# ── Frontend environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development needs NO variables: requests are same-origin and the Vite dev
# server proxies /api and /socket.io to the backend (http://localhost:4000).
#
# Deployment (separate static host + API host) — set at BUILD time, because
# Vite inlines import.meta.env.VITE_* into the bundle:
#
#   VITE_API_URL="https://your-api.onrender.com"   # no trailing slash
#
# Leave it unset and the build talks to its own origin (only correct when the
# API is served from the same host, e.g. behind a reverse proxy).

# Backend environment lives in backend/.env (see backend/.env.example).
